## Why this follow-up exists

The merged Phase 0–1 work established the correct local-commitment direction, but the interrupted session left documentation and code at different completion levels. This audit found that the later hardening merge recorded repairs in prose while several implementation seams still needed direct closure.

## What this PR repairs

- closes direct legacy-engine custody registration/replay bypass;
- rejects contradictory L1 network, persistence, digest, assurance, byte-length, and media-type assertions;
- makes the canonical browser commitment kernel race-safe so an older slow file hash cannot overwrite a newer selection;
- preserves the versioned local-commitment URL only as a compatibility re-export, not a duplicate runtime;
- replaces the stale v0.6 Ash HTML duplicate with a v0.7 compatibility route;
- removes new v0.7 claim-ceiling additions while leaving legacy v0.5/v0.6 vocabulary frozen for separate review;
- replaces receipt-list `innerHTML` with DOM/text construction;
- holds plaintext Cinder transport and rejects `fragment` / `candidateFragment` until Phase 6;
- prevents legacy v0.5 metadata hashes from being promoted into v0.7 L1 assurance;
- instantiates the full roadmap, implementation-status ledger, Phase 1 commitment ledger, and complete CI gates;
- preserves the existing Phase 0 live deployment probe rather than adding a duplicate probe.

## Roadmap honesty

Only Phases 0–1 are represented as implemented and hardened. Phase 4 reciprocal receipts and Phase 5 Relation Envelope remain Aperture-side designs/landing zones; Phase 6 Cinder transport remains held; Phases 2–3 and 7–9 remain planned, partial, or Open Field research.

## Verification completed

- exact SHA-256 vectors, empty file, mutation, and Unicode byte divergence;
- finite file-size hold and no-network browser kernel;
- stale-selection ordering;
- strict L0/L1 API validation;
- direct-engine bypass rejection;
- legacy replay non-promotion;
- raw fragment rejection;
- schema and duplicate-surface checks;
- Vercel rewrite/cache hygiene;
- Phase 0 deployment-probe contract;
- repository smoke and static-app suites.

## Current status

All repository CI gates are green on the current head. Vercel produced a ready preview. The PR remains a draft deliberately so the custodian can perform a final visual/interactive preview before merge.

